{"id": "De8phEeIRf3", "title": "Video by therishikatha", "description": "Are you doing AARTI the right way? 🪔 In temples, the lamp doesn’t just go round and round. It follows a path. 👇\n\n4 circles at His FEET\n2 at His NAVEL\n3 at His FACE\n7 round His WHOLE BODY\n\nThat’s the count in the temple worship manuals (Pancharatra Pradipa, Arcana Paddhati). Many families circle the face just once, and traditions differ, so tell us yours below!\n\nThe flame: ghee or camphor, with an ODD number of wicks (Hari Bhakti Vilasa 8.298).\n\nAnd the best part: forgot the mantras, or got the steps wrong? In the Skanda Purana, Shiva tells Parvati that when you do the aarti, the whole puja becomes complete:\n“mantrahīnaṁ kriyāhīnaṁ yat kṛtaṁ pūjanaṁ hareḥ / sarvaṁ sampūrṇatām eti kṛte nīrājane śive”\n(quoted in the Hari Bhakti Vilasa 8.302)\n\nSo tonight, let your child hold the lamp and count with you: 4, 2, 3, 7. 🙏\n\n📚 Want more stories of our gods for your kids? Our picture books, Books 1–3, are a set of 3 for ₹500 at rishikatha.com (link in bio).\n\n💾 Save this for your next aarti, and share it with someone who leads the aarti at home.\n💬 Face: ONCE or THREE times? Comment 1 or 3!\n\n#aarti #aartiritual #puja #pujavidhi #hinduism sanatandharma hindutemple vishnu diya hindurituals indianparents hindukids rishikatha templeculture spirituality", "channel": "therishikatha", "uploader_id": "22569163881", "uploader": "Rishi Katha", "timestamp": 1792996535, "like_count": 280183, "comment_count": 582, "http_headers": {"User-Agent": "Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 10.0; Win64; x64) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/146.0.0.0 Safari/537.36", "Accept": "text/html,application/xhtml+xml,application/xml;q=0.9,*/*;q=0.8", "Accept-Language": "en-us,en;q=0.5", "Sec-Fetch-Mode": "navigate", "Referer": "https://www.instagram.com/"}, "formats": [{"format_id": "dash-1384496803464127a", "ext": "m4a", "tbr": 58.424, "asr": 44100, "format_note": "DASH audio", "container": "m4a_dash", "vcodec": "no